{"availability":"available","full":"jralmaraz/wimse-identity-fabric","name":"wimse-identity-fabric","description":"Workload Identity in Multi-System Environments Identity Fabric — Proof of Concept","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-30T15:55:29Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:49:04Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://wimse-identity-fabric.pages.dev/enterprise.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:46.286Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:46.286Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:46.286Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T18:43:05.006Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T19:33:46.286Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Go implementation of the IETF WIMSE (Workload Identity in Multi-System Environments) standard, built as an incremental six-phase PoC. It demonstrates the complete workload identity stack: token issuance, workload-to-workload authentication over mutual TLS, cross-trust-domain token exchange, selective disclosure credentials, and OpenID Federation 1.0 for dynamic cross-domain trust — all with an interactive browser demo compiled to WebAssembly.","Modern cloud-native deployments span multiple trust domains — different clouds, clusters, and platforms — each with its own identity system. WIMSE defines how workloads (services, jobs, functions) prove their identity to each other without relying on a single shared secret or a centralised identity broker at request time.","This PoC implements two complementary mechanisms:"],"features":["Standard PoC — 10-chapter interactive story running live WASM crypto in your browser","Enterprise Demo — Identity sprawl, WIMSE solution, IdP integration patterns (Okta, Entra ID, Keycloak, Vault), centralised vs distributed, secrets management"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jralmaraz/wimse-identity-fabric/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fd560492e39647f378e43